    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d797">

                <pb facs="0883" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Harriman, W. Averell/74</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stettinius</hi>)<anchor n="64" xml:id="d797-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-05-23">May 23, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In talking to me yesterday afternoon before preparing to leave to return to his
                    post, Ambassador Harriman said the President requested him to do the following: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Tell Stalin the President is still hopeful that he can find a
                            satisfactory solution to the Polish problem, that it will be kept out of
                                <pb facs="0884" n="874" xml:id="pg874"/> “politics” and to express
                            the hope that the Soviets would give the Poles “a break”.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Discuss with Molotov the Finnish situation<anchor n="66"
                                xml:id="d797-f2"/> in an endeavor to ascertain if there is any other
                            possible action which could be taken which has not already been
                            attempted.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E[<hi rendition="#small-caps">dward</hi>] S[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >tettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d797-f1" n="64" type="source" xml:id="d797-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to the Director of the Office of European Affairs (Dunn) and the Deputy
                    Director (Matthews).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d797-f2" n="66" xml:id="d797-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence regarding the failure of Finland to withdraw from the war with
                    the Soviet Union, see <ref target="frus1944v03#pg_556">vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 556</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
